Subject: simple: don't wait for metadata of cancelled software ISP outputs

With the software ISP a request only completes once its buffers are done
and its metadata has been processed. SoftwareIsp::stop() cancels the output
buffers of the frames still in flight, but the IPA is stopped by then and
never produces metadata for them. conversionOutputDone() did not drop the
metadata requirement for cancelled or errored buffers (unlike the raw
capture error path in imageBufferReady()), so those requests were never
completed, remained in queuedRequests_, and PipelineHandler::stop() hit
ASSERT(data->queuedRequests_.empty()). Applications such as GNOME Camera
(through PipeWire/WirePlumber) aborted whenever a stream was stopped with
frames in flight, e.g. when switching cameras.

Upstream master has the same logic.

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
index efaba09b8..afb979f60 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -1034,6 +1034,19 @@ void SimpleCameraData::conversionOutputDone(FrameBuffer *buffer)
 
 	/* Complete the buffer and the request. */
 	Request *request = buffer->request();
+
+	/*
+	 * When the software ISP stops, it cancels the output buffers of the
+	 * frames still in flight and never produces metadata for them. Don't
+	 * wait for metadata that cannot arrive, or the request would stay
+	 * queued forever and PipelineHandler::stop() would assert on it.
+	 */
+	if (buffer->metadata().status != FrameMetadata::FrameSuccess) {
+		SimpleFrameInfo *info = frameInfo_.find(request->sequence());
+		if (info)
+			info->metadataRequired = false;
+	}
+
 	if (pipe->completeBuffer(request, buffer))
 		tryCompleteRequest(request);
 }
